<title>ITALY: Impregilo in Malawi hydroelectric deal.</title>
<headline>Impregilo in Malawi hydroelectric deal.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian construction group Impregilo, as sponsor of a 50 percent joint venture with Salini, said it will build a hydroelectric plant 70 km south of Blantyre for the Electricity Supply Commission of Malawi.</p>
<p>Construction of the 70 billion lire plant at Kapichira on the Shire River, entirely financed by the World Bank, will begin in October and will last 35 months, Impregilo said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
